{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c1255d04-5741-4c83-8034-7563901b7174","status":"SUCCESS","response":"{\n  \"doc_id\": \"keepass\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-001\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"KeePass must be downloaded and installed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Omits the target platform/operating system, version, distribution source, actor responsible for installation, and the precondition scope (which features or actions require installation).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-002\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"has no limits in length. A whole sentence can be used with more than 100 characters.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'No limits in length' is ambiguous as to whether a minimum length is also absent (allowing an empty password), and the illustrative phrase 'A whole sentence can be used' leaves unclear which characters (e.g., spaces, punctuation, Unicode) are permitted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-002\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_value_or_unit\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Master Password has no limits in length\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify a minimum password length, any practical/testable upper bound, or the supported character set and encoding.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-003\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"syntactic\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Folder selected must be of type the database can read and that is “name”.kdb\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Poorly structured phrasing conflates a 'Folder' (directory) with a '.kdb' file, states that 'the database can read' the file rather than the application reading the database file, and does not clarify whether '“name”' is an arbitrary filename placeholder or whether '.kdb' is case-sensitive.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-003\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Folder selected must be of type the database can read and that is “name”.kdb\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify the system's behavior if a user selects a file or folder that is not a valid readable '.kdb' file (e.g., filtering the selection dialog, rejecting the file, or displaying an error message).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-004\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the previews one will be replace if selected\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Contains typos ('previews' for 'previous', 'replace' for 'replaced') and unclear referents: it is ambiguous whether 'the previews one' means a previously created database in the same directory or anywhere, and whether 'if selected' refers to choosing the same name, selecting the existing file, or confirming an overwrite prompt.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-004\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Databases must have different names or else the previews one will be replace if selected\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify the scope of name uniqueness (same directory vs. global, case sensitivity) or whether the system warns the user and requests confirmation before overwriting an existing database.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-005\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"There must be entries in the database in order for them to be printed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify what happens if the user attempts to print when the database contains no entries (e.g., disabling the print option or showing an error/warning message), nor whether printing applies to all entries or selected entries/groups.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-006\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"All data related to the word must be shown.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'All data related to the word' is vague: it does not define what 'related to' means (substring, exact, or case-insensitive matching), whether 'All data' includes displaying sensitive fields such as passwords in plaintext or only listing matching entries, and refers to 'the word' without an antecedent while the example uses a substring ('abc').\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-006\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_condition\",\n      \"evidence\": \"All data related to the word must be shown.\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify which entry fields are searched, whether matching is case-sensitive, how matching data (especially passwords) is formatted or masked, or what happens when no matching entries are found.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-007\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A name is required in order for the new group/subgroup to be created\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify what the system does if the user tries to create a group or subgroup with an empty or whitespace-only name, nor any naming constraints (maximum length, allowed characters, or uniqueness).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-008\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A subgroup cannot be created when no group is selected\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify how the system enforces this restriction when no group is selected (e.g., disabling the subgroup creation control or displaying an error message).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-009\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"A name is required in order for the group/subgroup to be renamed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify what happens when a user attempts to rename a group or subgroup with an empty or whitespace-only name (e.g., rejecting the change, reverting to the previous name, or showing an error), nor valid naming rules.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-010\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"In order to find something in a group a word must be placed in the find field\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'something' does not specify what items or entry fields are searched, and 'a word' is ambiguous as to whether a whole word is required or any character, substring, or multi-word query is accepted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-010\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"a word must be placed in the find field\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify what happens if a user triggers a search with an empty find field, how search results are displayed, or whether subgroups are included in the search.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-011\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"syntactic\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An entry must belong to a group to be created\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Awkward phrasing is ambiguous as to whether a group must already be selected prior to creating an entry (as in KP-008) or whether the user can select or assign a group during the creation flow.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-011\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"An entry must belong to a group to be created\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify how the system behaves if a user attempts to create an entry when no group exists or no group is selected (e.g., disabling entry creation, prompting to select a group, or assigning a default group).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-012\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"When the password field is completed the repeat password field must be completed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"'the password field' and 'the repeat password field' lack an explicit antecedent/context, leaving unclear whether this applies to entry passwords, master passwords, or both; 'completed' is also vague as to whether empty/whitespace values count.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-012\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"When the password field is completed the repeat password field must be completed\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify the system's response if the password field is filled in while the repeat password field is left blank (e.g., preventing save or displaying a validation error).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-013\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"referential\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Password field and repeat password field must be identical\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Does not specify which screen or entity ('Password field and repeat password field') this applies to—entry creation/editing, master password setup, or both.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"KP-013\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Password field and repeat password field must be identica